Z||000004||theogre||10-08-2000||11:30 PM||||Shortening an auto shifter isn't a big deal. How it will look and how short you can go depend on what knob you have on top. I've seen this done to other GM cars that have basically the same shifter.<P>The Fiero's stock knob likely isn't going to let you get much shorter than stock without binding the boot up. There are shorter T handles and aftermarket knobs that will fit without reaching so far down the shifter.||||reg||1
